    description: "WHAT. With the language pack's Agda grammar (PR #2200), 13 real signatures in agda-stdlib are lost in files whose tree has NO error or missing node, so no partial_parse disclosure names them. 8 of the 13 are in Reflection/AST/AlphaEquality.agda, where lines 104-309 are glued into the type of the signature on line 103.\n\nCONSEQUENCE. The disclosure that tells a consumer a file was read through error recovery is silent for these files; the symbols are absent with no signal.\n\nCONTEXT. 510 of 1,248 agda-stdlib files still parse through error recovery (747 before the grammar switch); that share is WI-vimof-zusor-gilap-vusis-budab-vifas-nazos-talat's subject. This item is the part error recovery does not announce.\n\nNOT DONE. No detector was built (candidate: a signature whose type spans more lines than the layout rule allows).\n\nFound during PR 2 of the stable-id plan (the v15 bump), 2026-11-16 (PR #2200). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/STATUS.md."  # 0a20
